rom Cinema 4D (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from houdini (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-houdini\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-houdini-beta-2\">Publish from Houdini (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from solidworks (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-solidworks\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-solidworks-beta-2\">Publish from SolidWorks (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from spline, and figma (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-spline\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-spline-and-figma-beta-2\">Publish from Spline, and Figma (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"camera paths and default walkthroughs\" href=\"/docs/guides/camera-paths\" id=\"lnk-camera-paths-and-default-walkthroughs-2\">Camera paths and default walkthroughs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"hotspots and doors\" href=\"/docs/guides/hotspots-and-doors\" id=\"lnk-hotspots-and-doors-2\">Hotspots and doors</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse capture: film a room (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/film-a-room\" id=\"lnk-verse-capture-film-a-room-beta-2\">Verse Capture: film a room (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse play: host a web game\" href=\"/docs/guides/host-a-web-game\" id=\"lnk-verse-play-host-a-web-game-2\">Verse Play: host a web game</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"spatial bench\" href=\"/docs/guides/spatial-bench\" id=\"lnk-spatial-bench-2\">Spatial Bench</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"light and dark theme\" href=\"/docs/guides/light-and-dark-theme\" id=\"lnk-light-and-dark-theme-2\">Light and dark theme</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"share privately with tokens\" href=\"/docs/guides/share-privately\" id=\"lnk-share-privately-with-tokens-2\">Share privately with tokens</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"show your clients who looked\" href=\"/docs/guides/analytics\" aria-current=\"page\" id=\"lnk-show-your-clients-who-looked-2\">Show your clients who looked</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed anywhere: wordpress, shopify, webflow\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-anywhere\" id=\"lnk-embed-anywhere-wordpress-shopify-webflow-2\">Embed anywhere: WordPress, Shopify, Webflow</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse for commerce: 3d on product pages (woocommerce, magento, bigcommerce, salesforce)\" href=\"/docs/guides/commerce\" id=\"lnk-verse-for-commerce-3d-on-product-pages-w-2\">Verse for Commerce: 3D on product pages (WooCommerce, Magento, BigCommerce, Salesforce)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse links and embeds: embed the viewer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-the-viewer\" id=\"lnk-verse-links-and-embeds-embed-the-viewer-2\">Verse links and embeds: embed the viewer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"export a flythrough video\" href=\"/docs/guides/export-video\" id=\"lnk-export-a-flythrough-video-2\">Export a flythrough video</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"collect client review comments\" href=\"/docs/guides/collect-review-comments\" id=\"lnk-collect-client-review-comments-2\">Collect client review comments</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"author a guided tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/author-a-guided-tour\" id=\"lnk-author-a-guided-tour-2\">Author a guided tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"video on surfaces, sound in the room\" href=\"/docs/guides/video-and-audio\" id=\"lnk-video-on-surfaces-sound-in-the-room-2\">Video on surfaces, sound in the room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from ifc or usd\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-ifc\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-ifc-or-usd-2\">Publish from IFC or USD</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"upload fbx and obj\" href=\"/docs/guides/upload-fbx-obj\" id=\"lnk-upload-fbx-and-obj-2\">Upload FBX and OBJ</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"build a configurator\" href=\"/docs/guides/build-a-configurator\" id=\"lnk-build-a-configurator-2\">Build a configurator</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"present a scene to a room\" href=\"/docs/guides/present-a-scene\" id=\"lnk-present-a-scene-to-a-room-2\">Present a scene to a room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse-prepare: the local compression step\" href=\"/docs/guides/verse-prepare\" id=\"lnk-verse-prepare-the-local-compression-step-2\">verse-prepare: the local compression step</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"tune quality knobs\" href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-2\">Tune quality knobs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"run your own server\" href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-2\">Run your own server</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"monitor production\" href=\"/docs/guides/monitor-production\" id=\"lnk-monitor-production-2\">Monitor production</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"ask verse, the site assistant\" href=\"/docs/guides/ask-verse\" id=\"lnk-ask-verse-the-site-assistant-2\">Ask Verse, the site assistant</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: floor plan to 3d home\" href=\"/docs/guides/floor-plan-to-3d\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-floor-plan-to-3d-home-2\">Verse Home: floor plan to 3D home</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/instant-home\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-plan-to-a-home-buyers-walk-re-2\">Verse Home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page\" href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-one-tag-any-page-2\">&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"designer tools: framer, webflow, figma\" href=\"/docs/guides/designer-tools\" id=\"lnk-designer-tools-framer-webflow-figma-2\">Designer tools: Framer, Webflow, Figma</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"react and vue wrappers\" href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue-wrappers-2\">React and Vue wrappers</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"rest client round trip\" href=\"/docs/guides/rest-client\" id=\"lnk-rest-client-round-trip-2\">REST client round trip</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with woocommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-woocommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-woocommerce-2\">Sell with WooCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with bigcommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-bigcommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-bigcommerce-2\">Sell with BigCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with magento / adobe commerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-magento\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-magento-adobe-commerce-2\">Sell with Magento / Adobe Commerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in wix\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-wix\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-wix-2\">Embed in Wix</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in squarespace\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-squarespace\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-squarespace-2\">Embed in Squarespace</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in framer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-framer\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-framer-2\">Embed in Framer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in ghost and hubspot\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot-2\">Embed in Ghost and HubSpot</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with zapier\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-zapier-2\">Automate with Zapier</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with make\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-make-2\">Automate with Make</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with n8n\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-n8n-2\">Automate with n8n</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-10\"><h2>Blog & updates</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"all posts\" href=\"/docs/blog/index\" id=\"lnk-all-posts-2\">All posts</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"how verse streams a building\" href=\"/docs/blog/how-verse-streams-a-building\" id=\"lnk-how-verse-streams-a-building-2\">How Verse streams a building</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.7: what's new for you\" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"show-your-clients-who-looked\">Show your clients who looked<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#show-your-clients-who-looked\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p>Studio&#39;s <strong>Analytics</strong> page answers the questions a developer or an agency\ngets asked after sending a walkthrough link: how many people opened it, how\nlong they stayed, which rooms they spent time in, whether they got as far as\nasking about the property, and on what devices. Every number can be\nexported as a CSV or sent as a printable report.</p>\n<p><strong>You need:</strong> a Studio account and scenes you own (see\n<a href=\"/docs/guides/share-privately\" id=\"lnk-share-privately\">Share privately</a> for accounts and owned uploads).</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-open-the-dashboard\">1. Open the dashboard<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#1-open-the-dashboard\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-2\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Sign in at <code>/studio</code> and click <strong>Analytics</strong> in the top bar, or open a\nscene&#39;s <strong>Analytics</strong> panel and pick <strong>Full analytics &amp; client report</strong>.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>All scenes</strong> (the default) adds up every scene you own and lists each one\nwith its views, unique viewers, median time and enquiries. Click a scene to\ndrill into it.</li><li><strong>7 / 30 / 90 days</strong> picks the range. Days are UTC.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Number</th><th>What it counts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Views</td><td>each time the link was opened in a browser tab</td></tr><tr><td>Unique viewers</td><td>different browsers (a random id the browser keeps; no name or login)</td></tr><tr><td>Returning viewers</td><td>browsers that opened the scene more than once in the range</td></tr><tr><td>Median / total time</td><td>time the scene was open <strong>and on screen</strong> (sampled every 2 s; a tab left in the background does not count)</td></tr><tr><td>Enquiries</td><td>clicks on the scene&#39;s enquiry button</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"2-add-an-enquiry-button\">2. Add an enquiry button<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#2-add-an-enquiry-button\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-3\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The last step of the funnel is your call to action. On a scene&#39;s analytics\npage, under <strong>Enquiry button</strong>, set a label and a link:</p>\n<ul><li><code>https://…</code> — your contact form, a booking page or a WhatsApp link\n(<code>https://wa.me/91…</code>)</li><li><code>mailto:sales@yourcompany.com</code></li><li><code>tel:+91 80 1234 5678</code></li></ul>\n<p>Every viewer of that scene then sees the button over the walkthrough. The\nfunnel reads <strong>Opened → Interacted</strong> (dragged, tapped, walked or pressed a\nkey) <strong>→ Stayed 30 s+ → Enquired</strong>.</p>\n<p>The same setting over the API:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"sh\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-sh\">curl -X PUT https://HOST/v1/scenes/SCENE/enquiry -H &quot;Authorization: Bearer TOKEN&quot; \\\n  -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#39;{&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Book a site visit&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://wa.me/918012345678&quot;}&#39;</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"3-where-people-looked-and-which-rooms-they-saw\">3. Where people looked and which rooms they saw<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#3-where-people-looked-and-which-rooms-they-saw\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-4\">#</a></h2>\n<p>For an interior with a floor plan, the scene page shows:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Where people looked:</strong> a heatmap over the plan. Blue cells show where\nvisitors stood; amber cells show where they waited for the scene to load.</li><li><strong>Rooms visited:</strong> the plan is split into rooms at the doorways (open-plan\nspaces stay one room, corridors are their own). A room takes the name of a\nhotspot inside it (author one per room in the default experience, see\n<a href=\"/docs/guides/author-a-guided-tour\" id=\"lnk-author-a-guided-tour-3\">Author a guided tour</a>), otherwise &quot;Room 1&quot;,\n&quot;Room 2&quot;… from largest to smallest. Rooms nobody entered are listed with 0,\nwhich is also worth knowing. Time spent on a terrace or in the garden reads\n<strong>Outdoors</strong>; time spent looking at the house from the opening overview\nreads <strong>Overview (outside the floor plan)</strong>.</li><li><strong>Name your rooms:</strong> click a room on the plan (or ✎ in the list) and type\n&quot;Kitchen&quot;, &quot;Master bedroom&quot;… The name is used everywhere: dashboard, CSV\nand client report, for past days too.</li><li><strong>Top viewpoints:</strong> the five spots where visitors spent the most time, as\n&quot;Kitchen · facing north-west&quot;, with numbered pins on the plan.</li></ul>\n<p>A scene without an interior floor plan (an object, an open-air scene) has no\nrooms; the dashboard says so and still shows where people looked.</p>\n<p>Scenes plan the storey you start on, with interior walls\nand the garden marked; re-upload an older multi-storey scene (a new version)\nto get its rooms.</p>\n<h2 id=\"4-devices\">4. Devices<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#4-devices\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-5\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Phone / tablet / desktop, iOS / Android / desktop systems, the in-app\nbrowser (Instagram, Facebook, WhatsApp, LinkedIn…) and how people arrived:\na direct link, a <a href=\"/docs/guides/share-privately\" id=\"lnk-private-share-link\">private share link</a> or an embed on\nyour site. People opening a share link are counted, but stay anonymous like\neveryone else.</p>\n<h2 id=\"5-send-it-to-your-client\">5. Send it to your client<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#5-send-it-to-your-client\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-6\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Download CSV</strong> gives the same numbers as a spreadsheet: headline\nmetrics, one row per day, the funnel, rooms and device split (and, for\nAll scenes, one row per scene).</li><li><strong>Client report</strong> opens a clean one-page report for the scene (or all\nscenes) and range. Press <strong>Print / Save as PDF</strong>: it prints on white\npaper, A4, with how it was measured at the bottom.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"6-share-a-viewer-report-with-a-link\">6. Share a viewer report with a link<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#6-share-a-viewer-report-with-a-link\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-7\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The <strong>viewer report</strong> is the client-ready page for one scene: who opened it\n(anonymous viewers, how many times, on what device, and where they came from:\nWhatsApp, Instagram, Google, an e-mail, your website&#39;s embed…), the time spent in\neach room as a heatmap over the floor plan, the hotspots they opened, how many\nquestions they asked Ask Verse, average and median time, and the funnel to your\nenquiry button. It works on a phone.</p>\n<ol><li>In <strong>Studio → Analytics</strong>, pick the scene and press <strong>Share report</strong> (or\nopen <strong>Client report</strong> and press <strong>Share link</strong>).</li><li>Name the link after who it is for (for example &quot;Sharma family&quot;), pick the\nwindow (last 7, 30 or 90 days) and press <strong>Create link</strong>.</li><li><strong>Copy</strong> the link and send it. It is shown once — the server keeps only a\nfingerprint of it.</li><li>To stop sharing, press <strong>Revoke</strong> next to the link. It stops working at\nonce, for the page and the CSV alike. Deleting the scene revokes every link.</li></ol>\n<p>Anyone with the link sees the report and can download its CSV. They never see\nyour account, your other scenes or your enquiry link. If the scene is\n<strong>private</strong>, the report still opens but does not link to the scene or show the\nfloor-plan image — the rooms are drawn from their outlines instead — so a\nreport link never becomes a way into a private scene. Viewers appear as codes\nlike <code>V-4AF8C3</code>: one code is one browser, never a name.</p>\n<p>The same exports over the API: <code>GET /v1/scenes/&lt;id&gt;/analytics.csv?days=30</code>\nand <code>GET /v1/account/analytics.csv?days=30</code>; the viewer report is\n<code>GET /v1/scenes/&lt;id&gt;/report[.csv]</code>, its links <code>/v1/scenes/&lt;id&gt;/report/links</code>\n(<a href=\"/docs/api#analytics\" id=\"lnk-api\">API</a>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"privacy-in-short\">Privacy, in short<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#privacy-in-short\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-8\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li>No names, e-mail addresses, phone numbers or IP addresses are stored for\nanalytics. A visitor is a random id their browser keeps in local storage;\nthe server keeps only a keyed hash of it.</li><li>Device class, system and in-app browser are worked out **on the\ndevice**; the browser&#39;s user-agent string is not stored with the\nanalytics rows.</li><li>Visitors with <strong>Do Not Track</strong> or <strong>Global Privacy Control</strong> switched on are\nnever counted. A link with <code>?analytics=0</code> is not counted; <code>?analytics=never</code>\nturns counting off on that browser for good (<code>?analytics=1</code> turns it back\non); an embed with <code>analytics: false</code> is never counted.</li><li>Storage is bounded: raw samples live in a rotating log; completed days\nare kept as daily totals per scene for <code>VERSE_ANALYTICS_KEEP_DAYS</code> (400\ndays by default) and then deleted. Deleting a scene deletes its analytics.</li></ul></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/guides/analytics\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div><aside class=\"docs-toc\" id=\"asd-docs-toc\"><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><a href=\"#1-open-the-dashboard\" id=\"lnk-1-open-the-dashboard\">1. Open the dashboard</a><a href=\"#2-add-an-enquiry-button\" id=\"lnk-2-add-an-enquiry-button\">2. Add an enquiry button</a><a href=\"#3-where-people-looked-and-which-rooms-they-saw\" id=\"lnk-3-where-people-looked-and-which-rooms-th\">3. Where people looked and which rooms they saw</a><a href=\"#4-devices\" id=\"lnk-4-devices\">4. Devices</a><a href=\"#5-send-it-to-your-client\" id=\"lnk-5-send-it-to-your-client\">5. Send it to your client</a><a href=\"#6-share-a-viewer-report-with-a-link\" id=\"lnk-6-share-a-viewer-report-with-a-link\">6. Share a viewer report with a link</a><a href=\"#privacy-in-short\" id=\"lnk-privacy-in-short\">Privacy, in short</a></aside></section>"}